me="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1024176A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIPPON CATALYTIC CHEM IND</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIPPON SHOKUBAI CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ADACHI YOSHIFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HARADA NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAYAMA TOSHIMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAMOTO SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ADACHI, YOSHIFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARADA, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAYAMA, TOSHIMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAMOTO, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A novel cross-linked polymer composition swelling in water which is excellent in the rate and amount of brine absorption under pressure. The composition comprises a mixture of a particulate cross-linked polymer which swells in water and is basic in water and a particulate cross-linked polymer which swells in water and is acidic in water. When water is present among the particles of the two particulate polymers, the polymers are united with each other through ionic bonds formed by the neutralization of at least part of the acid groups of the particulate polymer which is acidic in water with the particulate polymer which is basic in water.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur une nouvelle composition polymère réticulée qui présente un excellent taux et une excellente vitesse d'absorption de saumure sous pression. Cette composition comprend un mélange d'un polymère réticulé particulaire qui gonfle dans l'eau et est basique dans l'eau et d'un polymère réticulé particulaire qui gonfle dans l'eau et est acide dans l'eau. Lorsqu'il y a de l'eau dans les particules des deux polymères particulaires, ces polymères sont réunis par des liaisons ioniques formées par neutralisation d'au moins une partie des groupes acides du polymère particulaire qui est acide dans l'eau avec le polymère particulaire basique dans l'eau.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>